{"title":"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #15</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #12</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If snow falls at a rate of 1 mm every 6 minutes, then how many hours will it take for 1 m of snow to fall?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a29bbd9f1ad7518a236a68337d89421be27420a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\  33 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 60 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 26 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 10 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"442\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> m is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> mm, so it will take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baa1b437c3cb051fb2a632ca654d15def780d3b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 1000 = 6000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" /> minutes for all of the snow to fall. This is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91ffd4a1dafdaf31df6b549ebfcd593b66c3646e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6000}{60} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } 100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"139\" height=\"38\" /> hours.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" sty